# %[1]s

A [rastrillo](https://amadan.net/rastrillo/rastrillo) app. Before
writing app code, read the framework's skill at the version this app
builds against:

    cat "$(go list -m -f '{{.Dir}}' amadan.net/rastrillo/rastrillo)/SKILL.md"

then, before each piece of work, the `skill/` topic its index names for
it. Never another copy from the module cache: an older SKILL.md
describes a framework this app is not built on.

## Layout

- `internal/<app>/`: `app.go` (`App`, `New`), `routes.go` (every
  route), `handlers.go` (actions), `models.go`, `migrations.go`,
  `render.go`, `api.go` (`/api/v1`), and `static/`, served by the app.
- `internal/<app>test/`: tests through the real handler. Write the
  failing test here first.
- `manifest/`: optional, a screen set per manifest, generated into
  `gen/` (never edit; run `rastrillo generate`). manifest/README.md
  mounts the first.

## Code

`make code` (`rastrillo budget code`) holds Go to four limits:

- lines at most 80 columns, a tab reaching the next stop of 4;
- non-test files at most 400 lines;
- non-test functions at most 40 lines; an action,
  `func(*action.Visit)`, 15;
- no one-letter names but a capital type parameter and the testing
  types' `t`, `b`, `f`.

1. Spell names out, except those, `err` and `ctx`: `request`, not `r`.
2. Name things for what the person is doing (`entries.Publish`), not
   how the code does it (`saveEntry`).
3. One route, one intent: two buttons that mean two things post to two
   routes.
4. An action has four beats: read the input, run one operation, answer
   a refusal, say what success looks like.
5. Operations hold the rules and the database work, return `op`
   refusals and never touch HTTP.
6. A helper answers refusals; success stays written out in the action.
7. Comments say why, in one or two full sentences, never what the code
   does.

The rest, and what each gate message means:

    cat "$(go list -m -f '{{.Dir}}' amadan.net/rastrillo/rastrillo)/skill/code.md"

## Rules the family holds hard

- Every query touching user-owned rows goes through `scope.Owned` —
  reads AND writes, transactions included. A row that isn't yours 404s,
  never 403s.
- Never bind a request body onto a GORM model: explicit
  `map[string]any` + `.Select` allowlist.
- Every page and form goes in `Routes`' guarded group, which checks
  CSRF by origin. The API sits outside it: a bearer token is its only
  credential.
- The API cannot see page middleware: a page's rule beyond ownership
  (admins only, say) goes in `api.go`'s `authorize` too, or a token
  gets around it.
- Money is a whole number of the currency's smallest unit, stored with its ISO 4217 code beside it, and shown with `money`. A float never touches a value a person will be held to.
- Screens work with JavaScript disabled; destructive actions get their
  own confirm-page URL.

## Schema

- Edit models.go, run `rastrillo migration generate`, and read the SQL:
  it may rebuild a table. Write a rename by hand with
  `rastrillo migration new rename_x`: generate sees a drop and an add.
  Never edit a migration that has shipped; they apply at boot, once.
- A subsystem's schema goes in `BootSchema`, in the order it applies,
  `migrate.Merge(sessions.Schema, apitoken.Schema, Schema)`, and never
  in `Schema`, which generate and check diff against the models.

## Growing

- Sign-in: `skill/signin.md`. With `*sessions.Sessions`, keep
  `NewTokenPage(database, sessions)` on `App` and call
  `app.tokens.Mount(guarded)` in `Routes`' page group.
- Past 5,000 lines, split by feature: `internal/<app>/<feature>` with
  `func Mount(routes *action.Routes, deps *Deps)`, called from the
  app's `Routes`, the one function of that name.

## The gate

- `make ci` runs vet, gofmt, staticcheck, govulncheck, gitleaks, the
  budgets, `make code`, `make routes` (every action is mounted), the
  tests, perf, and the migration and generate checks, as CI does. Run
  it before every push. If that is too slow, a budget has failed: fix
  it, never skip the gate. While editing: `go test -short ./...`.
- Budgets: 5,000 source and 8,000 test lines per directory, 10s per
  test package, 150ms to first byte per GET screen, 500ms cold boot
  (timing fails only on CI). An exception goes in
  `.rastrillo/budgets.txt` or `code.txt`, with its reason.
- `TestMain` calls `budget.Main`; each test starts with `t.Parallel()`
  (perf excepted) and copies the `dbtest` template.
- The two `TestIndex` tests check the placeholder index: behind sign-in
  they get a 303, so repoint or delete them. `TestPerfScreens` then
  needs `Signin`, and a `{param}` route a `Paths` entry it seeds.
- A test whose inputs Go cannot see (it runs `go build`, reads outside
  its package, uses the network) gets its own target with `-count=1`.
- `CGO_ENABLED=0` throughout: the stack is cgo-free.
- Raise the Makefile's `GOTOOLCHAIN` with each Go security release.

## Serving

`rastrillo.Resolve` + `Serve` speak the CARLOS activation contract;
`./app -addr :8080` serves anywhere. The framework answers `/healthz`
and `/api/version`. The CSRF check and, with accounts, the cookies go
by `<APP>_ORIGIN`. Under a hub's `/<slug>`: README.md's Deploy and
`skill/data.md`.
